A||N||4||fierobaby||dew strips||||12||
Z||000000||fierobaby||06-16-2001||12:20 PM||||Hey anyone know hwo to fix the dew strips on the windows? mione are all rotted away...well hope to hear from someone soon!<P><BR>Corinne<BR>Fiero baby||||reg||12
Z||000001||MrPBody||06-16-2001||12:39 PM||||A common problem.  Here's one set of instructions:  <A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/fierov6/OSG/dew-wipes.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nbci.com/fierov6/OSG/dew-wipes.html</A> .  You can probably find more info by searching.<P>Rodney Dickman sells a tool to remove two inaccessible screws.  <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com</A> <P>Good luck!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||btoth||06-16-2001||06:03 PM||||Yep, get Rodney's tool and you can order the replacements from the Fiero Store (that's were I got mine).  The tool came with instructions and sugestions on how to replace them.  Mine turned out to be a bit of a project... had a couple stubborn screws so I just tore the dew stip off from the screws and then unscrewed them.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  But putting the new ones on was easier than taking the old ones off I thought.||||reg||1
Z||000003||NASAReeves||06-16-2001||09:03 PM||||Order the replacement "dew strips" from:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsdirect.com" TARGET=_blank>www.gmpartsdirect.com</A> <P>..."& save a buck or two."<P>The part numbers are:<P>20606220 and 20606221  (outer left/outer right).  <BR>  <P>------------------<BR>Scott & Traci<BR>'88 GT||||reg||3
Z||000004||deceler8||06-17-2001||11:34 AM||||I was able to get mine from my local Chevy dealer for what I thought was a reasonable price (about $24 each).<P>Rodney's tool really works...looks so simple, but is exactly what you need for the job.||||reg||1
